{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTeLZ2NAmDSnJ1nm65nx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your answers settle round one, so this is the full reading before anything is drawn.\n\n**Question:** which statuses does a Roamstay booking pass through, and who sets Cancelled and No-show?\n**Outcome:** support can name who to ask for a Cancelled or a No-show booking.\n\n**Settled by your message and your answers**\n* Reader, question, outcome and type: a state diagram for support\n* Detail, audience and distance: Balanced, Mixed and Laptop\n* The five statuses, with Confirmed holding Upcoming and In stay\n* Who sets the two statuses you asked about: the guest cancels, the hotel marks No-show\n\n**Outline, in drawing order**\nSeven states: Pending, Confirmed, Upcoming, In stay, Completed, Cancelled and No-show.\n1. Start to Pending\n2. Pending to Confirmed: card authorised\n3. Inside Confirmed, start to Upcoming\n4. Upcoming to In stay: check in\n5. In stay to the end of Confirmed\n6. Confirmed to Completed: check out [from In stay]\n7. Pending to Cancelled: guest cancels\n8. Confirmed to Cancelled: guest cancels\n9. Confirmed to No-show: missed check-in [from Upcoming]\n10. Completed to end\n11. Cancelled to end\n12. No-show to end\n\n**Two framings**\n* A: one status map, with Confirmed as a section around Upcoming and In stay and all three final states on the right. It shows every exit and keeps the point that No-show only follows a missed check-in. I recommend this one\n* B: Confirmed as a single state with no inner states. It is simpler, but it loses the Upcoming and In stay split, so support could not see that a booking already in stay cannot become a No-show\n\n**The look**\n* Colour marks Cancelled, through a `%% focus:` line. The request names two states equally and I recommend Cancelled because two moves reach it\n* No zone lines. Confirmed is already a section\n* Title \"Roamstay booking status\", with the subtitle \"Every status a booking passes through, and who sets Cancelled and No-show\"\n* Source line: the booking status description from the request, with the gaps below named\n* Two single stickies: \"Set by the guest, while the booking is Pending or Confirmed\" on Cancelled and \"Set by the hotel, after a missed check-in\" on No-show\n\n**Left out:** a failed card authorisation, a Pending booking that expires, a hotel or system cancellation and a refund, because none of them is in your description.\n\n**Assumed, and what would settle each**\n* Cancelled, No-show and Completed are final: a bookings doc\n* Check-in is the move from Upcoming to In stay, and check-out leaves from In stay: a bookings doc\n* A guest can cancel from In stay, because you said Confirmed as a whole: your correction\n* Your message is current behavior: a bookings doc\n\n**Still open:** nothing beyond the assumptions above.\n\nIs this the right reading of the board?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_read_input_tokens":99387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ae87e4d-87f8-4f96-996f-f78a55638582","uuid":"c0714722-a63e-4903-b255-4d0bd2b4e14a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T23:55:25.999Z","request_id":"req_011CgTeLYba62BmGH2yaTrPt"}
